{
  "kanji": "水",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 水\ntitle: water\njlpt: 5\ntags: [jlpt-n5, grade-1, pictograph, starter]\nstrokes: 4\nradical: 水\nradicalNumber: 85\nonyomi: [スイ]\nkunyomi: [みず, みず-]\ndistractors: [火, 川, 木]\n---\n\n# 水 — water\n\n**Strokes:** 4 · **Key (radical):** 水 (no. 85) · **JLPT:** N5 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n水 is a pictograph of flowing water: a central stream with droplets or currents on either side. It is one of the\nmost productive key components. On the left side of a kanji it shrinks to the three-drop form 氵 (さんずい), as in\n海, 池, 泳, 洗. In 氷 (ice) the character is recognisably 水 with one extra stroke.\n\nIt is also one of the \"five elements\" in the weekday names: 水曜日 (Wednesday) goes with 火 ([火](火.md)), [木](木.md), 金 and 土.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| スイ | on | 水曜日 すいようび, [水中](../words/水中.md) すいちゅう, 水道 すいどう, 香水 こうすい |\n| みず | kun | 水 みず (water), 水着 みずぎ, 水色 みずいろ |\n| みず- | kun | prefix before a word, e.g. 水玉 みずたま |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [水中](../words/水中.md) すいちゅう — underwater\n- [山水](../words/山水.md) さんすい — landscape (mountains and water)\n- 水 みず — water (cold water; hot water is お湯 おゆ)\n\n## Notes\n\nJapanese distinguishes cold 水 from hot お湯 and from 氷 (ice); English \"water\" covers all three, so learn the\nseparate words. For rivers see [川](川.md).\n",
